#. Tag: title
#: interface.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "The interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: interface.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browse and View modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: interface.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "By default, &kappname; opens in Browse mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: interface.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this mode you can easily navigate through your files and folders. As you "
"can see on the screenshot, the preview window shows the current image as "
"well as any embedded image comment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: interface.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browse Mode Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: interface.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From the Browse mode, unchecking <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Return</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Browse</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> will "
"put you in View mode, where the image takes all the space of the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: interface.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Mode Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: interface.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can start directly in View mode by starting &kappname; with an image as "
"an argument."
msgstr ""

